{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgNeu1obIPmM12lYvM5RI","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking for a plan for a fashion e-commerce storefront built in Figma at 1920px width, with 11 frames and a component library. The button is a horizontal auto-layout component, so its text centers itself; the text field is a vertical auto-layout with a Label and an Input.\n\nI start with tokens: brand black #000000, ink #111111, body #55555A, muted #8A8A90, line #E7E7E4, surface #F7F6F3, white; sale/wine #A62B2B, rating gold #D9A441, urgency #C0562E, free-ship success #2F7D5B. Fonts are Volkhov for the wordmark and headings and Poppins for UI. The grid is 1920 wide, content max 1600, margins 160, and radius is 10 for buttons, 16 for cards, 24 for sections. The type scale runs display 96/100, section 48/58, H2 36/44, H3 24/32, body 16/28, small 14/24, caption 12/18, eyebrow 12 SemiBold with 0.16em tracking, and price 18 SemiBold.\n\nI plan to build reusable components before screens: Header/Home and Header/Store at 96 tall with a centered Poppins 14 nav and a current-item underline, three 20px icons plus a cart with a count text layer; Footer/Home and Footer/Store on cream; Block/FeatureStrip (4 columns, icon 28, title 15 SemiBold, muted 14); Card/Product with a 3:4 portrait photo at radius 16, name, price, an old price and a SOLD OUT badge toggle; Card/Testimonial; Block/Newsletter; Block/Instagram (7 photos); Block/CollectionBanner with hotspots for Flat Cap, Cotton Shirt, Suspender, Leather Shoes and \"Men Collection\", \"Classic Gentleman\", Size M, $100.00, Buy Now; Block/Deals with countdown 02 Days 06 Hr 05 Mins 30 Sec, 3 slides and card \"01 — Spring Sale\" \"30% OFF\"; Button variants built from the given Button plus an Outline and a Light; a Checkbox with checked/unchecked; QuantityStepper; Breadcrumb; and Auth/Shell.\n\nFrames sit in a row at x = 0, 2100, 4200, 6300, 8400, 10500, 12600, 14700, 16800, 18900, 21000: 01_Home, 02_Shop, 03_Product, 04_Mini_Cart, 05_Cart, 06_Checkout, 07_Sign_Up, 08_Sign_In, 09_Forgot_Password, 10_Confirmation_Code, 11_New_Password. For 04_Mini_Cart I build 03_Product fully, then clone it, rename, resize to 1920×1080, set clipsContent so the page reads as an inactive background under the dim overlay, and add the 480-wide drawer plus a cart count of 1. The auth frames at 1920×1080 use one Auth/Shell instance with the form fields placed on top, so Sign Up keeps First Name, Last Name, Email Address, Phone Number, Password and Confirm Password.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation_input_tokens":40966,"input_tokens":1,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":40966}},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"45b716de-dcc2-45d2-a4d3-f5e780ce57d2","uuid":"873ee922-03c2-4993-94db-0e2c31d9f309","timestamp":"2026-11-01T20:00:53.890Z","thinking_duration_ms":72432}
